schema_version: 2
catalogs:
  - provider: claude
    backend: cli
    selection_mode: full
    source_cli: Claude
    cli_version: 2.1.296
    last_updated: 2026-10-14
    notes:
      - Model list, every model's effort line and every row's value re-read 2026-10-03 by an
        agent-operated capture of the Claude Code 2.1.288 `/model` picker (Windows UI Automation
        visible text, checked against screenshots); the list, effort lines and defaults equal the
        2026-09-30 capture of 2.1.285. Scope is the operator's subscription account on one machine;
        entitlement elsewhere is unverified.
      - "Evidence: docs/research/fixtures/claude-2.1.288/model-picker.agent-capture.redacted.txt,
        docs/research/fixtures/claude-2.1.288/model-row-status.redacted.txt,
        docs/research/fixtures/claude-2.1.285/model-picker-12-rows.agent-capture.redacted.txt,
        docs/research/fixtures/claude-2.1.285/model-row-status.redacted.txt and
        docs/research/2026-10-03-claude-picker-2-1-288.md"
      - The twelve source rows are Default (recommended), Opus 5.5, Fable 5.1, Sonnet 5.5, Haiku 4.5,
        Sonnet 5, Opus 5, Fable 5, Opus 4.8, Opus 4.7, Opus 4.6, and Sonnet 4.6. The picker shows eight
        rows at a time and scrolls the rest. Default is a provider-default sentinel, not an executable
        model id; its row and effort branch remain in evidence. Cats exposes the eleven explicit rows
        in picker order, with Opus selected by default as the operator requested earlier. This does
        not claim a provider-default alias will always resolve to Opus.
      - "Display names are the exact picker labels, which carry the model version. Cats adds the
        status suffix ` (default)` in lowercase across model and effort menus; it is not part of the
        model name."
      - "Execution values were observed per row: the agent chose a row for the session only (`s`,
        which left settings.json unchanged) and read the local `/status` Model line without
        submitting a prompt. On 2.1.285, Opus 5.5 sets `opus` (claude-opus-5-5), Sonnet 5.5 `sonnet`
        (claude-sonnet-5-5), and Sonnet 5 `claude-sonnet-5`. On 2.1.288 (2026-10-03) rows 2-12 were
        all re-read: Opus 5.5 `opus` (claude-opus-5-5), Fable 5.1 `fable` (claude-fable-5-1),
        Sonnet 5.5 `sonnet` (claude-sonnet-5-5), Haiku 4.5 `haiku` (claude-haiku-4-5-20251001),
        and each remaining row its full model id."
      - "The `sonnet` alias moved from claude-sonnet-5 (2.1.282) to claude-sonnet-5-5; the Claude Code
        2.1.284 changelog made Sonnet 5.5 the default Sonnet model. Entry `sonnet` keeps its id and its
        `sonnet` execution, so a saved selection keeps executing what it already did, and its label now
        follows the row that sets `sonnet`: Sonnet 5.5. Sonnet 5 is a new entry that executes
        `claude-sonnet-5`."
      - "The picker no longer offers an Opus (1M context) row. `--model opus[1m]` still resolved to
        claude-opus-5-5[1m] on 2026-09-26, but the operator chose to follow the picker: Opus now
        executes `opus`, and its 1M label and limit are removed. The standard context value was not
        observed, so no limit is recorded. The operator also chose the picker's `claude-fable-5-1`
        over the `fable` alias; both resolved to claude-fable-5-1. Entry ids are unchanged. On
        2.1.288 the Fable 5.1 row sets `fable` again (Claude Code 2.1.287: picking Fable now saves
        a value that follows the newest Fable). On 2026-10-03 the operator decided to keep
        `claude-fable-5-1`: the Fable 5.1 label then always matches the model that runs, while the
        alias would move to a newer Fable before the catalog is refreshed. Both still resolve to
        claude-fable-5-1."
      - "Effort is one picker-wide selection. For each adjustable row, the capture pressed Right until
        the line returned to its starting level. Opus 5.5, Fable 5.1, Sonnet 5.5, Sonnet 5, Opus 5,
        Fable 5, Opus 4.8, and Opus 4.7 cycle Low, Medium, High, xHigh, and Max; Opus 4.6 and Sonnet
        4.6 cycle Low, Medium, High, and Max only. Explicit `(default)` markers: Medium for Opus 5.5
        and Sonnet 5.5 (and Default), xHigh for Opus 4.7, and High for every other adjustable row.
        Haiku displays `Effort not supported for Haiku 4.5` and keeps `controls: []`. The Max usage
        warning is retained per model. Effort tokens reuse the retained `--effort` mapping of the
        earlier rows."
      - "Ultracode is no longer an effort level. Claude Code 2.1.284 made it a separate `/effort`
        toggle that no longer forces xhigh, and no 2.1.285 or 2.1.288 picker row offers it. The operator chose on
        2026-09-30 to follow the picker and remove it. The 2.1.285 parser still accepts
        `--effort ultracode` as a legacy alias of `xhigh`, so a session bound earlier keeps a valid
        argument."
      - Effort descriptions on Opus 5.5, Fable 5.1, and Sonnet 5.5 come from the Claude Code static
        artifact, not the picker. Low, Medium, High, and Max keep their earlier provenance and are
        unchanged in the 2.1.285 artifact; xHigh uses the 2.1.285 artifact text. The other rows carry
        only the observed Max warning.
      - Haiku 200K remains unverified 2.1.246 provenance. Context limits for the other rows were not
        observed and are omitted. Print mode (`-p`, which Cats uses) and other accounts were not
        probed.
      - The picker list appears to be remotely controlled. On 2026-09-26 the operator reported a
        twelfth row, which they called Opus 5.5 (1M), on another machine with the 2.1.282 build and
        the same Max account; the 2026-09-30 capture on this machine showed no such row. A shorter
        list later is not removal evidence, and an added row needs its own capture. See
        docs/research/2026-09-26-claude-picker-eleven-rows.md and
        docs/research/2026-09-30-claude-picker-sonnet-5-5.md.
      - "Refreshed 2026-10-14 from Claude Code 2.1.296 by an agent-operated /model capture (Claude Max sign-in, --safe-mode). The picker has 13 rows: Default plus 12 models. Haiku 5.5 is new (Low to Max, (default) Medium) and sets the `haiku` alias, which now resolves to claude-haiku-5-5; the Haiku 4.5 row sets claude-haiku-4-5-20251001 and supports no effort, so it moved to its own entry. Every other row kept its label, description, effort levels and (default) level. From 2.1.293 the effort line stops at both ends instead of wrapping; the capture walked each row to both ends. Max effort remains a level on every row that offered it. Evidence: docs/research/fixtures/claude-2.1.296/model-picker.agent-capture.redacted.txt."
    models:
      - default: true
        id: opus
        label: Opus 5.5
        capabilityTags:
          - tool_use
          - reasoning
        notes:
          - "Picker description: For complex work and everyday tasks"
          - "The Default (recommended) row describes Opus 5.5 - best for everyday, complex tasks, with
            the same effort cycle and Medium default."
          - Executes `opus` as the picker row does; `/status` showed claude-opus-5-5 without a `[1m]`
            suffix on 2.1.285. The 2.1.283 release notes say Opus already has a 1M context window,
            but no limit was observed, so none is recorded. The earlier `opus[1m]` execution and 1M
            label ended on 2026-09-26 by operator decision.
        source_names:
          - Opus
          - Opus 5 with 1M context
          - Opus 5.5 with 1M context
          - Opus 5.5
        execution:
          model: opus
        controls:
          - key: claude.reasoning_effort
            label: Reasoning effort
            description: Controls Claude Code effort for supported models.
            kind: enum
            scope: both
            values:
              - value: low
                label: Low
                description: Quick, straightforward implementation with minimal overhead
              - value: medium
                label: Medium
                description: Balanced approach with standard implementation and testing
              - value: high
                label: High
                description: Comprehensive implementation with extensive testing and documentation
              - value: xhigh
                label: xHigh
                description: Deeper reasoning than high, just below maximum (on supported models)
              - value: max
                label: Max
                description: Maximum capability with deepest reasoning. May use excessive tokens resulting in long
                  response times or overthinking. Use sparingly for the hardest tasks.
            semanticTags:
              - reasoning_intensity
            default: medium
      - default: false
        id: fable
        label: Fable 5.1
        capabilityTags:
          - tool_use
          - reasoning
        notes:
          - "Picker description: For your toughest challenges"
          - Executes `claude-fable-5-1`, the value the picker row set on 2.1.282; the operator chose it
            over the `fable` alias. On 2.1.288 the row sets `fable` (claude-fable-5-1); the operator kept
            `claude-fable-5-1` on 2026-10-03.
        source_names:
          - Fable
          - Fable 5.1
        execution:
          model: claude-fable-5-1
        controls:
          - key: claude.reasoning_effort
            label: Reasoning effort
            description: Controls Claude Code effort for supported models.
            kind: enum
            scope: both
            values:
              - value: low
                label: Low
                description: Quick, straightforward implementation with minimal overhead
              - value: medium
                label: Medium
                description: Balanced approach with standard implementation and testing
              - value: high
                label: High
                description: Comprehensive implementation with extensive testing and documentation
              - value: xhigh
                label: xHigh
                description: Deeper reasoning than high, just below maximum (on supported models)
              - value: max
                label: Max
                description: May use excessive tokens resulting in long response times or overthinking. Use
                  sparingly for the hardest tasks.
            semanticTags:
              - reasoning_intensity
            default: high
      - default: false
        id: sonnet
        label: Sonnet 5.5
        capabilityTags:
          - tool_use
        notes:
          - "Picker description: Most efficient for simpler tasks"
          - "`sonnet` resolves to claude-sonnet-5-5 on 2.1.285, as the Sonnet 5.5 picker row sets it. It
            resolved to claude-sonnet-5 on 2.1.282, when this entry was labelled Sonnet 5. The 1M
            `sonnet[1m]` alias is not offered by the picker and is not used here."
        source_names:
          - Sonnet
          - Sonnet 5
          - Sonnet 5.5
        execution:
          model: sonnet
        controls:
          - key: claude.reasoning_effort
            label: Reasoning effort
            description: Controls Claude Code effort for supported models.
            kind: enum
            scope: both
            values:
              - value: low
                label: Low
                description: Quick, straightforward implementation with minimal overhead
              - value: medium
                label: Medium
                description: Balanced approach with standard implementation and testing
              - value: high
                label: High
                description: Comprehensive implementation with extensive testing and documentation
              - value: xhigh
                label: xHigh
                description: Deeper reasoning than high, just below maximum (on supported models)
              - value: max
                label: Max
                description: May use excessive tokens resulting in long response times or overthinking. Use
