  - provider: codex
    backend: cli
    selection_mode: full
    source_cli: Codex
    cli_version: 0.162.1
    last_updated: 2026-10-14
    notes:
      - Complete visible model list and every per-model reasoning/advanced menu captured on 2026-10-01
        Asia/Taipei (2026-09-30 UTC) from Codex CLI 0.159.2 in Windows Terminal using UI Automation
        text and window screenshots.
        Scope is the local CLI account; entitlement on other accounts is unverified.
      - "Evidence: docs/research/fixtures/codex-0.159.2/picker.agent-capture.redacted.txt and
        docs/research/fixtures/codex-0.159.2/machine-catalog.redacted.json;
        docs/research/2026-10-01-codex-picker-gpt-6-1-sol.md records capture cost and validation."
      - The eight picker rows agree with the eight visibility=list entries from codex debug models.
        The hidden gpt-reserve and codex-auto-review entries are enumeration evidence, not Cats picker
        rows. GPT-6.1-Sol is newly offered first; no existing picker row was removed.
      - Display labels preserve the exact GPT-style casing now observed in the picker. Raw slugs
        remain execution.model. GPT-6.1-Sol is explicitly (default); Astra is only (current) in the
        per-invocation --model gpt-6-astra capture. This supersedes the earlier Astra model default.
      - Each model reasoning set/default was observed independently. GPT-6.1-Sol, Astra, GPT-6-Sol,
        GPT-5.6-Sol and GPT-5.6-Terra offer Max/Ultra; both Luna models offer Max only; GPT-5.5 ends
        at Extra high. GPT-6.1-Sol and GPT-5.6-Sol default to Low, all others to Medium.
      - The operator previously approved flattening More reasoning into one Cats effort list.
        Navigation, per-model usage warnings and advanced descriptions remain in the picker fixture.
        Max/Ultra display descriptions use the visible picker wording rather than the different
        machine enumeration descriptions.
      - Raw effort tokens/defaults and all eight 272000 context values were re-observed in codex debug
        models; these are CLI catalog values, not claims about OpenAI API limits. Older capability
        tags and migration source_names remain with their earlier provenance; no capability tags were
        inferred for new models.
      - "cli_version advanced from 0.159.2 to 0.160.0 on 2026-10-03 at the operator's request, without a new picker capture: `codex debug models` listed exactly this scope's 8 entries, with no other finding. Fields that source does not compare were not re-read, and the notes above describe the 0.159.2 evidence. Evidence: docs/research/fixtures/codex-0.160.0/model-list.probe.redacted.json."
      - "Refreshed 2026-10-14 from Codex CLI 0.162.1. `codex debug models` now marks gpt-5.5 visibility=hide ('Legacy coding model.'), and the agent-operated picker capture shows seven rows without GPT-5.5; the operator confirmed removing it, and it stays reachable as the custom model string gpt-5.5. The 0.162.1 picker shows no (default) marker on any row, so GPT-6.1-Sol is no longer the model default (operator-confirmed). Every remaining reasoning and More reasoning menu, label and description matched the 0.159.2 capture. Evidence: docs/research/fixtures/codex-0.162.1/picker.agent-capture.redacted.txt and docs/research/fixtures/codex-0.162.1/model-list.probe.redacted.json."
    models:
      - default: false
        id: gpt-6.1-sol
        label: GPT-6.1-Sol
        limits:
          contextWindowTokens: 272000
        notes:
          - Latest workhorse model for coding and everyday work.
        execution:
          model: gpt-6.1-sol
        controls:
          - key: codex.reasoning_effort
            label: Reasoning effort
            description: Controls Codex CLI reasoning depth for supported models.
            kind: enum
            scope: both
            values:
              - value: low
                label: Low
                description: Fast responses with lighter reasoning
              - value: medium
                label: Medium
                description: Balances speed and reasoning depth for everyday tasks
              - value: high
                label: High
                description: Greater reasoning depth for complex problems
              - value: xhigh
                label: Extra high
                description: Extra high reasoning depth for complex problems
              - value: max
                label: Max
                description: For difficult problems when quality matters more than speed · higher usage
              - value: ultra
                label: Ultra
                description: For demanding work using multiple agents · highest usage
            semanticTags:
              - reasoning_intensity
            default: low
      - default: false
        id: gpt-6-astra
        label: GPT-6-Astra
        capabilityTags:
          - tool_use
        notes:
          - Frontier intelligence for the most demanding work.
        source_names:
