  - provider: muse
    backend: cli
    selection_mode: full
    source_cli: Muse
    cli_version: 1.4.7-R6101.1
    last_updated: 2026-10-14
    notes:
      - "Model list re-read 2026-09-26 on Muse Code 1.4.0 (muse-bin-1.4.0-R4161.1): MSP `model/list`
        over `muse serve --no-session-log` (providerId `meta`, profileId `tbh`, source
        `providerCatalog`). Same four rows, limits, and descriptions; no additions or removals.
        Each row now carries ordered `variants` matching the curated per-model effort menus
        (both 1.3 rows through max, both 1.2 rows through xhigh); parser-only `none`/`ultra`
        remain excluded. Native picker traversal was attempted but incomplete on this Linux
        host (no wlrctl/wtype; pty stalled before render), so effort menus retain their
        2026-09-18 / 2026-09-25 provenance."
      - "Evidence: docs/research/fixtures/muse-1.4.0/model-list.agent-capture.redacted.txt and
        docs/research/fixtures/muse-1.4.0/picker-transcription.agent-capture.redacted.txt
        (limitation log). Full method: docs/research/2026-09-26-muse-picker-agent-capture.md."
      - "Model list re-read 2026-09-25 on Muse Code 1.3.0 (muse-bin-1.3.0-R3401.1): MSP `model/list`
        over `muse serve --no-session-log` (providerId `meta`, profileId `tbh`, source
        `providerCatalog`) plus an agent-operated `/model` picker capture (Windows UI Automation
        visible text, checked against private screenshots). Same four rows, limits, and descriptions;
        no additions or removals. The 1.3 `/effort` menu re-confirmed minimal, low, medium, high,
        xhigh, max in order with xhigh session-current and no default marker; other rows' effort
        menus retain their 2026-09-18 provenance."
      - "Evidence: docs/research/fixtures/muse-1.3.0/model-list.agent-capture.redacted.txt and
        docs/research/fixtures/muse-1.3.0/picker-transcription.agent-capture.redacted.txt.
        Full method: docs/research/2026-09-25-muse-picker-agent-capture.md."
      - First curated Meta Muse entry, added with the provider itself on 2026-09-05.
      - Model list read 2026-09-05 from muse's own `model/list` reply over the MSP host it serves on
        stdio (`muse serve`), which is its only enumeration surface - the CLI has no `models`
        subcommand and `muse exec` cannot list. The reply carried providerId `meta`, profileId
        `tbh`, and source `providerCatalog`, so the list is account-resolved and complete for this
        account.
      - "Evidence: docs/research/2026-09-05-meta-muse-cli-probe.md"
      - "`name` is the raw id `muse --model` accepts (the reply's `modelId`); `label` is a rendering
        of the reply's `displayLabel`, which upstream sets equal to the id."
      - The `-contributor` rows are the same models on terms Meta describes as "Your content,
        including inter-session messages, may be used for product improvement." They are listed so
        an operator can choose one deliberately.
      - No entry is marked default even though `model/list` flags `muse-spark-1.3-contributor` as
        `isDefault`. Projecting that here would make every runtime turn opt into content sharing
        without the operator asking for it; with no `--model` argument muse still uses whatever the
        account prefers.
      - "`context: 1007997` and `max_output: 128000` are the reply's `contextLimit` and
        `outputLimit`, identical across all four rows. `cost` is null upstream and is therefore
        omitted rather than guessed."
      - "Effort menus corrected from the operator on 2026-09-18: both 1.3 rows have minimal, low,
        medium, high, xhigh, max; both 1.2 rows stop at xhigh. No effort default is declared.
        Evidence: docs/research/fixtures/muse-unknown-version/efforts-2026-09-18.redacted.txt."
      - The earlier exec --help list proves parser vocabulary, not per-model picker
        availability/defaults. Model-list version, freshness, labels, and limits retain their
        2026-09-05 provenance; this correction only re-observes effort menus.
      - "cli_version advanced from 1.4.0-R4161.1 to 1.4.2-R4684.1 on 2026-10-03 at the operator's request, without a new picker capture: `muse-bin serve --no-session-log, MSP model/list` listed exactly this scope's 4 entries, with no other finding. Fields that source does not compare were not re-read, and the notes above describe the 1.4.0-R4161.1 evidence. Evidence: docs/research/fixtures/muse-1.4.2-R4684.1/model-list.probe.redacted.json."
      - "Refreshed 2026-10-14 from Muse Code 1.4.7 (muse-bin-1.4.7-R6101.1). MSP `model/list` and the /model picker both list three rows in this order: muse-wonder-1.0 (new; released 2026-10-12), muse-spark-1.3 and muse-spark-1.2. The two -contributor rows are gone from both; the settings file now carries a contributor_mode_enabled switch instead. The operator confirmed removing them; they remain reachable as custom model strings where Muse still accepts them. The /effort picker with muse-wonder-1.0 active lists minimal, low, medium, high, xhigh, max with no default marker (the highlighted xhigh is the session value); MSP variants agree. `model/list` now marks muse-wonder-1.0 isDefault, which is not projected as a curated default. Evidence: docs/research/fixtures/muse-1.4.7-R6101.1/model-picker.agent-capture.redacted.txt and docs/research/fixtures/muse-1.4.7-R6101.1/model-list.probe.redacted.json."
