  - provider: cursor
    backend: cli
    selection_mode: full
    source_cli: Cursor
    cli_version: 2026.10.01-e373342
    last_updated: 2026-10-14
    notes:
      - "The complete Cursor CLI 2026.10.01-e373342 model picker, replacing the 2026-09-18 shortlist at the operator's request on 2026-10-14: the 44 families of the account-resolved parameterizedModels reply in its order, without gemini-2.5-flash, which the CLI excludes. Captured with scripts/capture-cursor-parameterized-models.mjs, a process-local read of the reply `cursor-agent --list-models` already fetches; no installed file, credential or inference was involved. Evidence: docs/research/fixtures/cursor-2026.10.01-e373342/parameterized-models.redacted.json and docs/research/2026-10-14-shortlists-to-full.md."
      - "Each family's parameters are controls (cursor.context, cursor.effort, cursor.reasoning, cursor.reasoning_effort, cursor.thinking, cursor.fast) whose combinations select the server's exact variantStringRepresentation, passed as one --model argument. Enum values use the picker's display names; thinking and fast are the picker's on/off switches, here Off and On. A parameter with one value is fixed and not shown, as in the picker."
      - "Control defaults are the family's isDefaultNonMaxConfig variant, which the picker preselects when the user has no saved choice for that family."
      - "Claude Opus 5, GPT-5.5 and GPT-5.4 do not list every combination (thinking off has no Extra High or Max; 1M has no Fast), so each is split into two entries named like the picker's row summary (Claude Opus 5 No Thinking, GPT-5.5 272K, GPT-5.5 1M). No unlisted combination is offered."
      - "Max mode is a separate CLI setting (/max-mode), not a model choice, and is left to the CLI configuration. Legacy --list-models slugs remain custom strings."
    models:
      - id: default[]
        label: Auto
        execution:
          model: default[]
        controls: []
      - id: grok-4.7[context=256k,reasoning_effort=high,fast=true]
        label: Grok 4.7
        execution:
          model: grok-4.7[context=256k,reasoning_effort=high,fast=true]
          variants:
            - when:
                cursor.context: 256k
