  - provider: copilot
    backend: cli
    selection_mode: full
    source_cli: Copilot
    cli_version: 1.0.96
    last_updated: 2026-10-14
    basis:
      plan:
        label: Copilot Pro
    notes:
      - "Complete /model picker for a Copilot Pro account: 18 selectable rows (Auto plus 17 models). First captured 2026-09-27 (UTC+8) from GitHub Copilot CLI 1.0.88 on Windows native by operating the picker; the 2026-10-03 capture of 1.0.91 added Claude Sonnet 5.5 and moved gemini-3.6-flash, gemini-3.5-flash and kimi-k2.7-code to Unavailable models. Rows follow the 2026-09-27 recommended grouping in arrival order; Claude Sonnet 5.5 follows Claude Sonnet 5. Evidence: docs/research/fixtures/copilot-1.0.91/model-picker.agent-capture.redacted.txt, docs/research/fixtures/copilot-1.0.91/model-list.probe.redacted.json, docs/research/fixtures/copilot-1.0.88/model-picker.agent-capture.redacted.txt and docs/research/2026-09-27-copilot-picker-full-catalog.md."
      - "On 2026-10-03 the operator confirmed removing gemini-3.6-flash, gemini-3.5-flash and kimi-k2.7-code, which the 1.0.91 picker listed under Unavailable models (Your plan doesn't include this model). They remain reachable as custom model strings on plans that include them."
      - "The 1.0.91 picker lists 16 Unavailable models whose detail pane says the plan does not include them (gpt-6.1-sol, gpt-6-sol, gpt-6-astra, gpt-5.6-sol, gpt-5.5, claude-fable-5.1, claude-fable-5, claude-opus-5.5, claude-opus-5, claude-opus-4.8, claude-opus-4.8-fast, claude-opus-4.7, claude-sonnet-4.6, gemini-3.6-flash, gemini-3.5-flash, kimi-k2.7-code). They are omitted; users whose plan includes them can enter those IDs as custom model strings."
      - "The picker groups rows as Recent, Recommended, New and Other. The Recent group follows the account's recently used models, so a later capture can reorder the first rows without an upstream catalog change."
      - "IDs come from the models.list RPC, except the two Gemini rows, which models.list omits. On 2026-09-27 the operator confirmed gemini-3.8-flash and gemini-3.7-flash, and selecting Gemini 3.8 Flash printed Model changed from Auto to gemini-3.8-flash (medium)."
      - "Only GPT-5.6 Terra carries a (default) marker, so it is the only default row. Auto shows a check mark for the current session selection only."
      - "Reasoning, Context and Tier values follow each row's picker order. No value carries a default marker, so selection starts at the first value and always sends --effort, --context or --auto-tier, overriding the setting Copilot would otherwise use. Picker arrival values (mostly Medium, Auto Balance) were session state, not defaults. This follows the operator's 2026-09-27 instruction, as for Junie and Kiro."
      - "Context is a Tab toggle on the 11 rows that show two figures: the first figure is --context default and the second --context long_context. Figures are picker text, not token limits. Rows showing a dash have no context control."
      - "From 1.0.91 the picker shows a Category column (Versatile, Lightweight or Powerful) before Context. It is recorded in the evidence only."
      - "Detail-pane cost tiers and credits per 1M tokens are recorded per row in notes. Captured on Windows native only: WSL shares this scope, but a WSL installation and account may see different models. BYOK and custom providers are out of scope. Custom model strings remain available."
      - "Refreshed 2026-10-14 from Copilot CLI 1.0.96 (agent-operated picker capture with option cycles). The picker now has 19 selectable rows: Claude Haiku 5.5 (claude-haiku-5.5 from models.list; Low to Max reasoning, 100K/936K context) is new under Other models and sits before Claude Haiku 4.5 here, as in the picker. Every other row kept its label, reasoning order, arrival value and default marker. The Context figures changed on every row that has them and now equal the models.list contextMax/longContextMax values (for example GPT-5.6 Terra 272K/922K, was 400K/1.1M); labels and notes follow the new figures. Groups moved (GPT-6 Luna and Claude Sonnet 5.5 are Recommended; Claude Sonnet 5, Gemini 3.8 Flash and Grok 4.6 are Other), and the catalog keeps its 2026-09-27 order. The Unavailable group lists 12 models (claude-opus-4.7 is no longer shown). Evidence: docs/research/fixtures/copilot-1.0.96/model-picker.agent-capture.redacted.txt and docs/research/fixtures/copilot-1.0.96/model-list.probe.redacted.json."
    models:
      - id: auto
        label: Auto
        notes:
          - "Picker detail: Auto routes based on your task, real-time system health, and model performance. Auto is 10% off right now."
          - "Tier is the picker's routing profile. Its detail pane describes Efficiency, Balance and Intelligence; Fast appears only in the Tier cycle and --help. Arrival value was Balance, with no default marker."
        source_names:
          - auto
          - Auto
        execution:
          model: auto
        controls:
          - key: copilot.auto_tier
            label: Tier
            description: Auto routing profile, sent as --auto-tier.
            kind: enum
            scope: both
            values:
              - value: efficiency
                label: Efficiency
                description: "Favors faster models while preserving the quality needed for the task."
              - value: balance
                label: Balance
                description: "Balances model quality and speed while adapting to each task."
              - value: intelligence
                label: Intelligence
                description: "Favors stronger models for complex work while remaining adaptive for simpler tasks."
              - value: fast
                label: Fast
      - default: false
        id: grok-4.7
        label: Grok 4.7
        notes:
          - "Picker group: Recent models. Detail pane: Medium cost; credits per 1M tokens input 200, output 600, cache read 50, cache write 0."
          - "Picker context figures: 200K (default) and 500K (long_context). Long context raises the credits shown in the detail pane."
          - "Arrival reasoning value was High, with no default marker."
        source_names:
          - grok-4.7
          - "Grok 4.7"
        execution:
          model: grok-4.7
        controls:
          - key: copilot.reasoning_effort
            label: Reasoning
            description: Reasoning effort, sent as --effort.
            kind: enum
            scope: both
            values:
              - value: low
                label: "Low"
              - value: medium
                label: "Medium"
              - value: high
                label: "High"
              - value: xhigh
                label: "Extra High"
          - key: copilot.context
            label: Context
            description: Context window tier, sent as --context.
            kind: enum
            scope: both
            values:
              - value: default
                label: "200K"
              - value: long_context
                label: "500K"
      - default: true
        id: gpt-5.6-terra
        label: GPT-5.6 Terra
        notes:
          - "Picker group: Recent models. Detail pane: Medium cost; credits per 1M tokens input 200, output 1200, cache read 20, cache write 250."
          - "Picker row reads GPT-5.6 Terra (default); the marker is excluded from the label."
          - "Picker context figures: 272K (default) and 922K (long_context). Long context raises the credits shown in the detail pane."
          - "Arrival reasoning value was Medium, with no default marker."
        source_names:
          - gpt-5.6-terra
          - "GPT-5.6 Terra"
          - "GPT-5.6 Terra — Medium"
        execution:
          model: gpt-5.6-terra
        controls:
          - key: copilot.reasoning_effort
            label: Reasoning
            description: Reasoning effort, sent as --effort.
            kind: enum
            scope: both
            values:
              - value: none
                label: "None"
              - value: low
                label: "Low"
              - value: medium
                label: "Medium"
              - value: high
                label: "High"
              - value: xhigh
                label: "Extra High"
              - value: max
                label: "Max"
          - key: copilot.context
            label: Context
            description: Context window tier, sent as --context.
            kind: enum
            scope: both
            values:
              - value: default
                label: "272K"
              - value: long_context
                label: "922K"
      - default: false
        id: mai-code-1.1-flash
        label: MAI-Code-1.1-Flash
        capabilityTags:
          - latency_optimized
        notes:
