  - provider: opencode
    backend: cli
    selection_mode: full
    source_cli: OpenCode
    cli_version: 1.19.0
    last_updated: 2026-10-14
    basis:
      channel:
        id: opencode-go
        label: opencode-go
    notes:
      - "The complete opencode-go channel of OpenCode 1.19.0, replacing the 2026-09-18 shortlist at the operator's request on 2026-10-14: every model `opencode models opencode-go --verbose --pure` lists that is not deprecated (the model dialog hides deprecated rows), in the dialog's order for a provider section, newest release first and then by name. Labels are the listed names. Evidence: docs/research/fixtures/opencode-1.19.0/model-list.probe.redacted.json and docs/research/2026-10-14-shortlists-to-full.md."
      - "Variant is the installed 1.19.0 Select variant dialog: Default, which sends no variant, then the model's own variants in listed order under their raw names. Models without variants open no dialog and have no control. The value travels as the native prompt's variant field."
      - "Without a search, the model dialog moves Favorites and Recent rows out of their provider section, so a picker reading must include those sections; the listing command is unaffected."
      - Other OpenCode providers are out of scope and remain available as custom provider/model strings.
    models:
      - id: opencode-go/cat-jam-free
        label: Cat Jam Free
        execution:
          model: opencode-go/cat-jam-free
        controls:
          - key: opencode.variant
            label: Variant
            kind: enum
            scope: both
            values:
              - value: default
                label: Default
              - value: low
                label: low
              - value: medium
                label: medium
              - value: high
                label: high
              - value: xhigh
                label: xhigh
