            scope: both
            values:
              - value: "off"
                label: Off
                description: No extended thinking
              - value: low
                label: Low
                description: Better latency, lighter reasoning
              - value: medium
                label: Medium
                description: Moderate thinking
              - value: high
                label: High
                description: Deep reasoning
              - value: max
                label: Max
                description: No constraints on thinking depth
            semanticTags:
              - reasoning_intensity
  - provider: pi
    backend: cli
    selection_mode: full
    source_cli: Pi
    cli_version: 1.2.0
    last_updated: 2026-10-03
    basis:
      channel:
        id: openai-codex
        label: openai-codex
    notes:
      - "The openai-codex (ChatGPT subscription) channel of Pi 1.0.0: the models in the installed pi-ai registry (identical to the local model store refreshed 2026-10-03) that a ChatGPT account can run. Labels are the bare model ids, since the scope basis shows the openai-codex channel (operator decision 2026-09-29, replacing the <id> [openai-codex] labels); rows keep registry order; the selector only moves the current and a configured default model to the top. Other Pi providers are out of scope and remain available as custom provider/model strings."
      - "The channel list is Pi's build-time catalog, not account entitlement. Pi also lists gpt-5.3-codex-spark, which is omitted: the same ChatGPT account's Codex CLI lists (0.156.1 on 2026-09-24, 0.160.0 on 2026-10-03) did not include it, and a Cats turn selecting it failed on 2026-09-29 with \"The 'gpt-5.3-codex-spark' model is not supported when using Codex with a ChatGPT account.\" It remains reachable as a custom provider/model string. gpt-6.1-sol, new in Pi 1.0.0, is in that Codex 0.160.0 list."
      - "Thinking values per row are Pi's getSupportedThinkingLevels over each model's thinkingLevelMap, in Pi's order, labeled with Pi's tokens and thinking-selector descriptions. gpt-6-astra and gpt-6.1-sol have no off. Pi sends minimal as the low reasoning effort on every row here."
      - "Pi's thinking selector marks the default thinking level (settings defaultThinkingLevel, or the built-in medium when unset), so medium is the control default. The model selector marks only a user-configured default model, so no row is a default and the UI initializes the first row."
      - "Execution uses --provider openai-codex --model <raw ID> --thinking <level>. Limits are the registry contextWindow and maxTokens."
      - "Evidence: docs/research/2026-09-27-pi-openai-codex-full-catalog.md, docs/research/fixtures/pi-0.87.1/openai-codex-models.redacted.json and docs/research/fixtures/pi-1.0.0/model-list.probe.redacted.json."
      - "cli_version advanced from 1.0.0 to 1.2.0 on 2026-10-14 at the operator's request: the probe read the installed 1.2.0 package and found exactly this scope's 8 entries with the same per-model thinking levels and medium default. gpt-5.3-codex-spark is still listed and stays omitted, as acknowledged. Evidence: docs/research/fixtures/pi-1.2.0/model-list.probe.redacted.json."
