  - provider: auggie
    backend: cli
    selection_mode: full
    source_cli: Auggie
    cli_version: 0.36.0
    last_updated: 2026-10-14
    notes:
      - "Complete 36-row /model picker, captured 2026-10-03 (UTC+8) from Auggie 0.36.0 on Windows native by operating the CLI picker (first capture 2026-09-27, 34 rows). Rows follow picker order; IDs come from auggie model list --json, whose 36 displayName values equal the picker labels one to one. Evidence: docs/research/fixtures/auggie-0.36.0/model-picker.agent-capture.2026-10-03.redacted.txt, docs/research/fixtures/auggie-0.36.0/model-list.probe.redacted.json, docs/research/fixtures/auggie-0.36.0/model-picker.agent-capture.redacted.txt and docs/research/2026-09-27-auggie-picker-full-catalog.md."
      - "Pass id literally to --model. IDs are opaque; Prism rows use butler_a and butler_b. On 2026-09-27 each of the 34 rows was selected once in the picker and reported Using model: <label>; GPT-6.1 Sol and Claude Sonnet 5.5 (2026-10-03) are matched by exact displayName and were not selected."
      - "Claude Opus 5.5 is the only row the picker marks (default) on 2026-10-03, and its JSON row has isDefault true; on 2026-09-27 both marked Opus 4.8. The settings file was byte-identical at both captures, so the marker is not the saved session model. The (current) suffix on the session model and the JSON envelope defaultModelId, which names no picker row, are not catalog defaults."
      - "Effort is not bound: the picker shows no effort for any row, and selecting a row opens no effort step, so controls stay empty. JSON effortLevels per model and the global --reasoning-effort flag are recorded in model notes and the research note only."
      - Capture covers this Windows native installation and account only. WSL shares this scope but may see different models. BYOK is out of scope. Custom model strings remain available.
      - "Refreshed 2026-10-14 on the same Auggie 0.36.0: auggie model list --json and the /model picker now have 37 rows. The only change is Claude Haiku 5.5 (claude-haiku-5-5, exact displayName match), shown sixth between Claude Opus 5.5 and Claude Sonnet 5.5; every other row kept its label, order, cost tier and description, and Claude Opus 5.5 is still the only (default) row. Evidence: docs/research/fixtures/auggie-0.36.0/model-picker.agent-capture.2026-10-14.redacted.txt and docs/research/fixtures/auggie-0.36.0/model-list-2026-10-14.probe.redacted.json."
