  - provider: junie
    backend: cli
    selection_mode: full
    source_cli: Junie
    cli_version: 26.9.22
    last_updated: 2026-10-03
    notes:
      - "Complete 18-row /model list and per-model effort cycles, captured 2026-10-03 from Junie
        26.9.22 (build 3419.29) by operating the CLI picker (first capture 2026-09-26, 15 rows,
        build 3419.7). Every row is on the JetBrains AI channel. Evidence:
        docs/research/fixtures/junie-26.9.22/model-picker.agent-capture.2026-10-03.redacted.txt,
        docs/research/fixtures/junie-build-3419.29/model-list.probe.redacted.json,
        docs/research/fixtures/junie-26.9.22/model-picker.agent-capture.redacted.txt and
        docs/research/2026-09-26-junie-picker-full-catalog.md."
      - "Picker names are the entry IDs and labels. --model accepts only aliases and setting IDs
        and rejects picker names as Invalid model, so each row executes as the setting ID that the
        installed JAR's ModelOption$Specific pairs with its exact display name, such as
        gemini-3.7-flash for Gemini 3.7 Flash. The picker row Default (Gemini 3.7 Flash) is the only
        row marked Default. Evidence: docs/research/2026-09-28-junie-execution-ids.md."
      - "Effort tokens are the JAR's EffortLevel wire ids (enum name lowercased): none, minimal,
        low, medium, high, xhigh, max. Values follow EffortLevel order, which puts None first; the
        Right-key ring alone cannot show that. Only low and medium have run through Cats, and
        --help lists only low, medium and high."
      - "No effort default is declared. The Effort cell showed each row's saved setting, not a
        default. Menus and runtime resolution start at each model's first value: None for
        GPT-5.6-LUNA, GPT-5.6-SOL, GPT-5.6-TERRA, GPT-6-LUNA and GPT-6-SOL, Minimal for Gemini
        3.6 Flash, and Low for the rest. Junie Lite shows ‹ None › as its only value (Right does
        not change it) and Junie saves effortPerModel junie-lite none, so its control has the
        single value none. Accepted by the operator on 2026-09-26."
      - BYOK channels selected with --provider are out of scope. Custom model strings remain available.
    models:
      - default: true
        id: Gemini 3.7 Flash
        label: Gemini 3.7 Flash
        capabilityTags:
          - latency_optimized
        notes:
          - "Picker description: Top-tier model, good for everyday work."
          - "Picker price per Mtok: $0.40 input, $2.40 output."
          - "Picker row text: Default (Gemini 3.7 Flash), with the badge 70% off."
        source_names:
          - Gemini 3.7 Flash
          - Default (Gemini 3.7 Flash)
          - Gemini 3.7 Flash — Medium
        execution:
          model: gemini-3.7-flash
        controls:
          - key: junie.reasoning_effort
            label: Effort
            description: Controls Junie CLI effort for supported models.
            kind: enum
            scope: both
            values:
              - value: low
                label: Low
              - value: medium
                label: Medium
              - value: high
                label: High
            semanticTags:
              - reasoning_intensity
      - id: Junie Lite
        label: Junie Lite
