  - provider: kiro
    backend: cli
    selection_mode: full
    source_cli: Kiro
    cli_version: 2.31.0
    last_updated: 2026-10-13
    notes:
      - "Complete 21-row model list with per-model effort levels and defaults, read 2026-10-13 from
        kiro-cli 2.30.0 on native Windows 11 through the V3 engine's ACP config_option_update
        (sent while creating a session; no prompt), which lists the same rows, order and effort
        rings as the 2.27.1 interactive picker capture of 2026-10-03 (first capture 2026-09-27,
        20 rows, kiro-cli-chat 2.24.1). Order and raw IDs equal kiro-cli chat --list-models.
        The 2.30.0 V3 picker, walked the same day without cycling effort, shows the same 21
        rows, order, IDs, credit rates and descriptions.
        Evidence: docs/research/fixtures/kiro-2.30.0/model-list.probe.redacted.json,
        docs/research/fixtures/kiro-2.30.0/model-picker.v3-agent-capture.redacted.txt,
        docs/research/2026-10-13-kiro-v3-catalog-refresh.md,
        docs/research/2026-10-13-kiro-v3-picker-capture.md and, for the picker rings,
        docs/research/fixtures/kiro-2.27.1/model-picker.agent-capture.redacted.txt and
        docs/research/2026-09-27-kiro-picker-full-catalog.md."
      - "id, label and execution.model are the raw model IDs, passed to --model. The 2.30.0 V3
        picker shows these raw IDs; the display names in the V3 config reply (for example Claude
        Opus 5.5) do not appear in it. auto is a Kiro routing option kept as row 1."
      - "No model default is declared. The V3 config reports auto as the current model, meaning
        only the session's selection. --list-models reports default_model auto (plain output:
        * = default); that is recorded here as reference only and is not a catalog default."
      - "Effort tokens are each row's effortLevels in the V3 config reply, which match the
        settings-panel ring of the 2.27.1 capture. Only the eleven rows with hasEffort carry
        kiro.reasoning_effort; rows without effort have controls: []. The low/medium/high/xhigh/max
        list in kiro-cli chat --help is global text, not per-model evidence."
      - "Effort defaults are each row's defaultEffortLevel in the V3 config reply, adopted on
        2026-10-13 under the operator's instruction to follow best practice: claude-opus-5.5
        medium, claude-opus-4.7 xhigh, every other effort row high. Selection starts at that
        default and always sends --effort, which overrides chat.modelDefaults in
        ~/.kiro/settings/cli.json. The 2.27.1 picker had shown no default marker. The 2.30.0 V3
        picker panel shows each row's current effort, not a marked default: it equals these
        defaults except where chat.modelDefaults saves another level."
      - "The V3 config reply marks claude-opus-5, claude-sonnet-5, claude-opus-4.8, claude-opus-4.7,
        claude-opus-4.6 and claude-sonnet-4.6 thinkingToggleable with thinking on by default,
        and the V3 picker panel shows thinking on for them. claude-opus-5.5 and claude-sonnet-5.5
        are not toggleable: the 2.27.1 picker showed their thinking as Always on for this model,
        and the 2.30.0 V3 picker shows n/a, Not available for this model, the same text as rows
        without thinking. kiro-cli has no thinking argument, so the adapter cannot pass it and
        the axis is not represented."
      - "Kiro 2.27.1 added a fallback row to every model's settings panel (none on every row:
        Answers for this model when it refuses or is unavailable). It selects another model
        rather than an option of this one, and it is not represented. The 2.30.0 V3 panel has
        no fallback row."
      - "Context limits are --list-models context_window_tokens. Descriptions and credit rates are
        the config reply text, unchanged from the picker. Read on Windows native only: WSL shares
        this scope, but a WSL installation and account may see different models. Custom model
        strings remain available."
      - "cli_version advanced from 2.30.0 to 2.31.0 on 2026-10-14 at the operator's request, without a new picker capture: kiro-cli chat --list-models and the V3 ACP probe listed exactly this scope's 21 entries in the same order, with the same effort levels and defaults. Labels are raw IDs, so no display field needed the picker. Evidence: docs/research/fixtures/kiro-2.31.0/model-list.probe.redacted.json."
    models:
      - id: auto
        label: auto
        limits:
          contextWindowTokens: 1000000
        notes:
          - "Picker description: Models chosen by task for optimal usage and consistent quality"
          - "Picker rate: 1.00x credits."
